/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Vus is the shear carried by vertical stirrups (N); fy is the stirrup steel strength (N/mm²) and 0.87 = 1/1.15; Asv is the total area of the stirrup legs (mm²), 2 × 50.3 = 100.5 mm² for two-legged 8 mm stirrups; d is the effective depth and 
   - The formula is the truss analogy in one line.
   - b is the beam width (mm); fy is the stirrup steel strength (N/mm²), not taken greater than 415 N/mm² in this rule; the other symbols are as above.
   - Minimum stirrups are required even when τv ≤ τc.
   - Maximum spacing of vertical stirrups is the least of 0.75 d and 300 mm; for stirrups inclined at 45° it is the lesser of d and 300 mm.
   - Design aids such as SP 16 tabulate τc against pt, and Vus/d = 0.87 fy Asv/sv for each stirrup size and spacing.
*/
