/* book exam traps: Subtracting τc,max b d instead of τc b d. τc,max is only the ceiling on τv; the concrete share is τc b d. | Leaving Vus in kN in sv = 0.87 fy Asv d/Vus. 79.35 kN must be 79,350 N, or the spacing comes out 1000 times too large. | Taking Asv as the area of one leg. For two-legged 8 mm stirrups Asv = 100.5 mm², not 50.3 mm². | Rounding the spacing up (251.5 mm to 260 mm) or forgetting the 0.75 d and 300 mm limits. Always round down and apply all three limits. | Leaving out stirrups where τv < τc. Minimum shear reinforcement is still required, except where τv < τc/2 or in lintels. */
